# nftables SSH Firewall Guide (Allow & Block SSH)

For:

* Red Hat Enterprise Linux
* Ubuntu
* OpenSSH
* nftables

This guide covers:

* Allow SSH
* Block SSH
* IPv4 + IPv6
* Secure vs insecure rules
* Allow selected IP/subnet
* SSH rate limiting
* Interface-based SSH
* Logging
* Forward chain SSH
* Advanced production security
* Delete commands for every rule

---

# 1. What is SSH?

SSH = Secure Shell

Default port:

```text
22/TCP
```

Used for:

* Remote Linux login
* Server administration
* SCP/SFTP
* Tunnels

---

# 2. Check SSH Service

## RHEL 9

```bash
sudo systemctl status sshd
```

---

## Ubuntu 24.04

```bash
sudo systemctl status ssh
```

---

# 3. Show Current nftables Rules

```bash
sudo nft list ruleset
```

---

# 4. Show Rules with Handles (Needed for Delete)

```bash
sudo nft -a list ruleset
```

Example:

```text
tcp dport 22 accept # handle 15
```

Delete:

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle 15
```

---

# 5. Allow SSH (Basic)

## ✅ Secure Basic Rule

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 accept
```

Description:

* Allows SSH access

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 6. ❌ Insecure Alternative

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input accept
```

Problem:

* Opens ALL ports/services
* Full firewall bypass

---

# Difference

| Secure     | Insecure        |
| ---------- | --------------- |
| SSH only   | Everything open |
| Controlled | No protection   |

---

# 7. Block SSH

## ✅ Secure

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 drop
```

Description:

* Blocks incoming SSH

WARNING:

* Can lock you out remotely

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 8. Reject SSH Instead of Drop

## ✅ Advanced Secure

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 reject
```

Description:

* Actively refuses SSH
* Faster client response

---

# Difference: DROP vs REJECT

| DROP           | REJECT                 |
| -------------- | ---------------------- |
| Silent discard | Sends refusal          |
| More stealthy  | Easier troubleshooting |
| Slower timeout | Faster response        |

---

# 9. Allow SSH From Specific IPv4 Address

## ✅ Secure

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ip saddr 192.168.1.100 tcp dport 22 accept
```

Description:

* Only trusted IP can SSH

---

## Block Others

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 drop
```

---

## Delete Rules

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 10. Allow SSH From Specific IPv6 Address

## ✅ Secure

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ip6 saddr 2001:db8::10 tcp dport 22 accept
```

---

## Block Others

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 drop
```

---

## Delete Rules

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

