# 11. Allow SSH From Subnet

## IPv4

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
```

---

## IPv6

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ip6 saddr 2001:db8::/64 tcp dport 22 accept
```

Description:

* Allows SSH from trusted network

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 12. ❌ Insecure SSH Access

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 accept
```

Problem:

* Entire internet can attempt SSH
* Brute-force attacks possible

---

# ✅ Better Alternative

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ip saddr 192.168.1.0/24 tcp dport 22 accept
```

---

# Difference

| Secure               | Insecure        |
| -------------------- | --------------- |
| Trusted network only | Entire internet |

---

# 13. SSH Rate Limiting (IMPORTANT)

## ✅ Production Secure Rule

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 ct state new limit rate 5/minute accept
```

Description:

* Limits brute-force attempts

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 14. ❌ Insecure No-Limit Rule

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 accept
```

Problem:

* Unlimited attack attempts

---

# Difference

| Secure                | Insecure           |
| --------------------- | ------------------ |
| Brute-force protected | Unlimited attempts |

---

# 15. SSH Interface-Based Security

Example:

* LAN interface = eth1
* WAN interface = eth0

## ✅ Secure

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input iif "eth1" tcp dport 22 accept
```

Description:

* SSH only from LAN

---

## ❌ Insecure

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 accept
```

Problem:

* Internet-wide SSH exposure

---

# Difference

| Secure   | Insecure        |
| -------- | --------------- |
| LAN-only | Public internet |

---

# 16. Allow Established SSH Connections

## ✅ Important Secure Rule

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ct state established,related accept
```

Description:

* Keeps active SSH sessions alive

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 17. Log SSH Attempts

## ✅ Secure Monitoring

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 log prefix "SSH: " accept
```

Description:

* Logs SSH activity

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

---

# 18. Block SSH Brute Force Aggressively

## ✅ Advanced Security

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 ct state new limit rate over 10/minute drop
```

Description:

* Drops excessive login attempts

---

## Delete Rule

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter input handle <ID>
```

