# 19. Forward Chain SSH Rules

Used when Linux system acts as router/firewall.

---

## Allow Forwarded SSH

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter forward tcp dport 22 accept
```

---

## Block Forwarded SSH

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter forward tcp dport 22 drop
```

---

## Delete Rules

```bash
sudo nft delete rule inet filter forward handle <ID>
```

---

# 20. Port Knocking Style SSH Restriction (Advanced)

## Allow temporary SSH after trusted source

Example concept:

* Allow only admin IP

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input ip saddr 203.0.113.10 tcp dport 22 accept
```

Description:

* Simpler alternative to port knocking
* Stronger than open SSH

