# 21. SSH on Custom Port

Example:

```text
2222
```

## Allow custom SSH

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 2222 accept
```

---

## Block old port 22

```bash
sudo nft add rule inet filter input tcp dport 22 drop
```

---

# Difference

| Secure-ish        | Less Secure          |
| ----------------- | -------------------- |
| Non-standard port | Default port exposed |

NOTE:

* Security through obscurity only
* Not replacement for real security

